{"name":"Woodland Sage","hex":"#a4a393","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"woodland","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a creature or object: growing, living, or existing in a woodland.","Having the character of a woodland."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Land covered with woody vegetation.","A low-density forest."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/woodland"},{"term":"sage","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Wise.","Grave; serious; solemn."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very wise person or spiritual teacher; someone of gravity and wisdom, especially, a teacher venerable for years, and of sound judgment and prudence; a grave or stoic philosopher."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Salvia nemorosa","blocks":[{"text":"Salvia nemorosa, the woodland sage, Balkan clary, blue sage or wild sage, is a hardy herbaceous perennial plant native to a wide area of central Europe and Western Asia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Salvia_nemorosa-IMG_3624.jpg/330px-Salvia_nemorosa-IMG_3624.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salvia_nemorosa"},{"title":"Woodland","blocks":[{"text":"A woodland is, in the broad sense, land covered with woody plants, or in a narrow sense, synonymous with wood, a low-density forest forming open habitats with plenty of sunlight and limited shade. Some savannas may also be woodlands, such as savanna woodland, where trees and shrubs form a light canopy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Woodland%2C_Bogside_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2215308.jpg/330px-Woodland%2C_Bogside_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2215308.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodland"},{"title":"Sage (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Sage is a grey-green resembling that of dried sage leaves. As a quaternary color, it is an equal mix of the tertiary colors citron and slate. The hex RGB color value of the adjacent sage swatch is BCB88A. For decades, some military flight jackets were made in sage green."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Sage_iPhone_17.jpg/330px-Sage_iPhone_17.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sage_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/%D0%9A%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%B0%2C_%D0%A2%D0%B0%D1%80%D1%83%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%81%D1%82%D0%B5%D0%BF%2C_%D0%A3%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%97%D0%BD%D0%B0.jpg/500px-%D0%9A%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%B0%2C_%D0%A2%D0%B0%D1%80%D1%83%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%81%D1%82%D0%B5%D0%BF%2C_%D0%A3%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%97%D0%BD%D0%B0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/%D0%9A%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%B0%2C_%D0%A2%D0%B0%D1%80%D1%83%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%81%D1%82%D0%B5%D0%BF%2C_%D0%A3%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%97%D0%BD%D0%B0.jpg/1280px-%D0%9A%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%B0%2C_%D0%A2%D0%B0%D1%80%D1%83%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%81%D1%82%D0%B5%D0%BF%2C_%D0%A3%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%97%D0%BD%D0%B0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/%D0%9A%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%B0%2C_%D0%A2%D0%B0%D1%80%D1%83%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%81%D1%82%D0%B5%D0%BF%2C_%D0%A3%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%97%D0%BD%D0%B0.jpg/500px-%D0%9A%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%B0%2C_%D0%A2%D0%B0%D1%80%D1%83%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%81%D1%82%D0%B5%D0%BF%2C_%D0%A3%D0%BA%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%97%D0%BD%D0%B0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign